From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:17:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban placement: malformed registry labels fail
 closed in label_machines

PR #2171 review nit (t_01a1d4be7c79b6e4, GitHub review 5890499417; card t_01a1d4c327277a9d).

label_machines evaluated `wanted <= set(entry.get("labels") or [])`. A registry entry whose
`labels` was a non-iterable truthy value (an int) raised TypeError instead of being skipped, and
a str matched its characters (`labels: "x"` carried label `x`). Since #2171 the named-machine
branch of _machine_picks_up also goes through label_machines (empty label set), so one malformed
entry would crash named heavy_route routing as well as pool/label-set liveness.

Fix: judge labels with kanban_placement_coordination._carries (a list of str, else the entry
does not qualify: fail closed). A missing or null `labels` stays an empty set, as before, so a
named machine without labels still picks up.

Proof (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_placement_labels_shape.py):
- RED on origin/main 99c1a5d454: 6 failed (`labels: 5` -> TypeError: 'int' object is not
  iterable; "x"/"pool:worker"/dict/tuple/[str, int] matched), 4 controls passed.
- GREEN: 3 files (labels_shape, placement, freshness) 280 passed; the 73 test files importing
  kanban_placement / kanban_placement_coordination: 2139 passed, 0 failed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
